---
config: tests/fresco.config
---

Frozen higher-rank argument executes (e3b)
{ sig id : forall a. (a) -> a fun id(x) { x } sig app : forall a, b. ((a) -> b) -> (a) -> b fun app(f)(x) { f(x) } sig poly : (forall a. (a) -> a) -> (Int, Bool) fun poly(f) { (f(42), f(true)) } app(fun(x) { poly(x) })(~id) }
args : --fresco
stdout : (42, true) : (Int, Bool)

External print executes in the initial Wild context
{ print("answer="); 42 }
args : --fresco
stdout : answer=42 : Int

An explicitly Wild function executes
sig emit : modal [Wild] ((String) -> ()) fun emit(x) { print(x) } emit("ok ")
args : --fresco
stdout : ok () : ()

A pure global signature rejects external print
sig emit : (String) -> () fun emit(x) { print(x) } emit("bad")
args : --fresco
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type error:.*

Numeric conversions and division execute
floatToInt(intToFloat(84 / 2))
args : --fresco
stdout : 42 : Int

External list primitives retain polymorphism
(hd([42]), hd([true]))
args : --fresco
stdout : (42, true) : (Int, Bool)

String primitives execute
strsub("answer", 0, 3)
args : --fresco
stdout : "ans" : String

XML conversion executes
stringToXml("answer")
args : --fresco
stdout : answer : List XmlItem

List cons executes
1 :: [2]
args : --fresco
stdout : [1, 2] : List Int

List concatenation executes
[1] ++ [2]
args : --fresco
stdout : [1, 2] : List Int

An unsigned parameter cannot be used at two types (c1a)
(fun(f) { (f(42), f(true)) })(fun(x) { x })
args : --fresco
exit : 1
stderr : @.*Type error:.*

A variant field keeps its quantified type
tests/fresco/polymorphic_variant.links
args : --fresco
filemode : true
stdout : (42, true) : (Int, Bool)
